# INVWINNA.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: the item form's
# notes.  Item 1's two lines show in view mode; item 3's memo of more
# than MEMO_MAXLINES lines shows read-only with INV's message, in view
# and in edit mode, where typing into it changes nothing and ESC asks
# nothing; item 2's notes, empty, are typed with CTRL-ENTER between the
# lines on the Notes page, OK refusing a line longer than MEMO_COLS and
# more than MEMO_MAXLINES lines, the message under the fields and the
# focus on the notes, then saved after the record (CTRL-TAB, as
# CTRL-PGDN, is the page's key, so a TAB can no longer be typed); a new item is added with
# notes; item 1's notes are as they were after those saves, and a CP437
# letter typed into them shows as typed; the end by Exit.  A saved item
# is not shown again: the save set its Updated date from the test
# machine's clock (INVWINNB.KEY shows saved notes again, on locations
# and service records).
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINNA.SNP is its snapshot.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER
# item 1 in view mode: its notes read-only, the focus on its ID
K ENTER
S VIEW1
K ENTER
# item 3: more than MEMO_MAXLINES lines, read-only with INV's message
K DOWN DOWN ENTER
S VIEW3
K ENTER CTRL-E
S EDIT3
K CTRL-SHIFT-TAB
T x
S TYPED3
K ESC
S LEFT3
# item 2: the notes reached from Category by their page, typed over two
# lines
K UP CTRL-E CTRL-SHIFT-TAB
S NOTES2
T Head cleaned
K CTRL-ENTER
T Belt replaced
S TYPED2
# a line of MEMO_COLS + 1 characters: refused, the notes selected
K CTRL-ENTER
T 1234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901
K ENTER
S LINE
# MEMO_MAXLINES + 1 lines: refused
K BS
T a
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER CTRL-ENTER
K ENTER
S LINES
# two lines again: OK saves them, and the list is fetched again
K BS
T Head cleaned
K CTRL-ENTER
T Belt replaced
K ENTER
S SAVED2
# a new item with notes: the record added, then its notes
K INS
T SYS
K CTRL-SHIFT-TAB
T Came with the box
K ENTER
S ADDED
K END
S END
# item 1's notes untouched by the saves; CP437 letters (82h, E1h)
K HOME ENTER
S VIEW1B
K ENTER CTRL-E CTRL-SHIFT-TAB CEND
T  caf‚ á
S OEMTYPED
K ESC
S ASKED
K Y
S DROPPED
K ALT-F X
